The-astrologer kept-watch one-night, and-there-appeared to-him * the-stature of-the-handsome-one, strutting in his-two-mantles,
and-pondered Gemini, when it-spread-out for-him * the-beauty of-loveliness, shining from his-two-flanks;
and-Saturn brought to-him the-blackness for-his-hair * and-granted-him the-colour of-musk on his-two-temples;
Mars gave to-him the-redness of-his-cheek * and-Sagittarius shoots the-arrow from his-two-eyelids;
and-Mercury gave-him an-excess of-his-cleverness * and-Abā al-Suhā the-gaze of-the-slanderers toward-him.
So-remained the-astrologer bewildered at-what he-saw * and-hurried and-kissed the-ground between his-two-hands.
